          Two steps. <span class="gradient-text"
            >No flags to remember.</span
          >
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-start">
        <ol class="space-y-6 list-none p-0 m-0">
          <li class="reveal flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div
              class="flex-shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-sm font-bold bg-lime/10 border border-edge-hover text-lime"
            >
              1
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-1">Launch the TUI</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-mute">
                Type <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">claude-multi</code
                > and hit enter. The menu lets you add an instance, pick a
                provider, paste your key, choose what to copy from your default
                Claude setup, and you're done. Arrow keys to move, enter to
                select, that's it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="reveal flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div
              class="flex-shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-mono text-sm font-bold bg-lime/10 border border-edge-hover text-lime"
            >
              2
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-1">Run your new alias</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-mute">
                The wizard prints something like <code
                  class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">claude-glm</code
                >. Run it. Every flag and slash command from <code
                  class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">claude</code
                > works exactly as you'd expect.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="reveal terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <span class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></span>
            <span class="terminal-title">setup</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <span class="term-out"># one command, then everything happens in the menu</span><br />
            <span class="term-prompt">$</span>
            <span class="term-cmd">claude-multi</span><br />
            <span class="term-out"> ▸ </span><span class="term-ok"
              >➕ Add new instance</span
            ><br />
            <span class="term-out"> Step 1 / 8 · Instance Name › </span><span
              class="term-str">glm</span
            ><br />
            <span class="term-out"> Step 2 / 8 · Provider › </span><span
              class="term-ok">GLM</span
            ><br />
            <span class="term-out"> Step 3 / 8 · API Key › </span><span
              class="term-str">••••••••••••</span
            ><br />
            <span class="term-ok"> ✓ Instance 'glm' created.</span><br />
            <br />
            <span class="term-prompt">$</span>
            <span class="term-cmd">claude-glm</span><span class="cursor-blink"
            ></span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-text-mute text-right">
            The whole flow lives in the menu. No subcommands, no flags, nothing
            to memorize.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
